        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.441,
            0.846,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": "2. For each of the questions below, choose the expression that describes the solution. Then simplify it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.483,
            0.847,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "(a) Maria bought 8 m of lace to decorate the bags she made for school. She used $\\frac{1}{4}$ m for each bag and finished the lace. How many bags did she decorate? (i) $\\begin{array}{c}8 \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\\\8 \\div \\frac{1}{4}\\end{array}$ (ii) $\\frac { 1 } { 8 } \\times \\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ (iii) (iv) ${ \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } \\div 8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.637,
            0.847,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "(b) $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ meter of ribbon is used to make 8 badges. What is the length of the ribbon used for each badge? (i) $8 \\times \\frac{1}{2}$ (ii) $\\frac { 1 } { 2 } \\div \\frac { 1 } { 8 }$ (iii) $8 \\div \\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ (iv) ${ \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\div 8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.767,
            0.847,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "(c) A baker needs $\\frac { 1 } { 6 } \\mathrm { k g }$ of flour to make one loaf of bread. He has 5 kg of flour. How many loaves of bread can he make? (i) $5 \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 6 } }$ (ii) ${ \\frac { 1 } { 6 } } \\div 5$ (iii) $5 \\div \\frac { 1 } { 6 }$ (iv) $5 \\times 6$"
        },
